# Line-ending conversion: OFF, for every file, deliberately.
#
# `* -text` tells git never to convert end-of-line markers. Every blob is stored
# and checked out byte-for-byte as it was committed, on every platform and at any
# value of core.autocrlf.
#
# Why not the conventional `* text=auto` (or `*.py text`):
#
# v1 was imported with a mixed CRLF/LF index. `exchange/engine.py`, v1's backend
# modules, its Dockerfile, requirements.txt and the .bat files are all stored
# CRLF; everything else is LF. Any `text` attribute would renormalise those blobs
# to LF on the next checkout and change their bytes. Phase 1's golden fixtures
# are captured from v1's engine and replayed against v2's, so that byte-identity
# is the safety net the whole rebuild rests on. Losing it silently is the
# expensive failure, and it would have shipped unnoticed under the obvious
# formulation. `* -text` is the only formulation that provably renormalises
# nothing.
#
# Textual diffing is unaffected: that is the `diff` attribute, not `text`.
#
# Normalising the repository to LF remains possible. It is a deliberate, separate
# change -- its own commit, after Phase 1's fixtures are captured and green --
# never a side effect of a move, a checkout or a fresh clone on a Windows default.
* -text
